From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: fix SM8150 HFI4 QP range enable mask

The external Test19 capture ends at the HFI4 QP_RANGE_V2 property. Its size
is the expected 84 bytes, but both enable masks are zero. Patch 0022
changed the packetizer from constant 7 to caller-provided fields. Those
fields were never initialized. Packet zeroing in 0032 made the error
deterministic.

Restore the HFI4 contract. Public min/max QP controls apply to I, P and B
frames, so both wire enable masks are 7. Log the packed ranges and layer
before submission so another reset has an unambiguous payload boundary.

The rest of the Test19 property sequence was re-audited for initialized
wire fields. No other restored H.264 admission property copies an unset
payload member. Keep the Test19 final-count and cache changes unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
index 7c676bb86cc4..4741d2d3471d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
@@ -1376,8 +1376,9 @@ pkt_session_set_property_4xx(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *pkt,
 		range->max_qp.qp_packed = max_qp;
 		range->min_qp.layer_id = in->min_qp.layer_id;
 		range->max_qp.layer_id = in->max_qp.layer_id;
-		range->min_qp.enable = in->min_qp.enable;
-		range->max_qp.enable = in->max_qp.enable;
+		/* The public V4L2 controls always apply to I, P and B frames. */
+		range->min_qp.enable = 7;
+		range->max_qp.enable = 7;
 		pkt->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(u32) + sizeof(*range);
 		break;
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 880682b7e9b6..7954af607b8d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1250,6 +1250,12 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst, bool set_work)
 			HFI_LAYER_ID_ALL : 0;
 		quant_range_v2.max_qp.layer_id =
 			quant_range_v2.min_qp.layer_id;
+		if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core))
+			dev_info(inst->core->dev,
+				 "venus-sm8150: encoder QP range min=%#x max=%#x layer=%#x enable=7\n",
+				 quant_range_v2.min_qp.qp_packed,
+				 quant_range_v2.max_qp.qp_packed,
+				 quant_range_v2.min_qp.layer_id);
 
 		ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &quant_range_v2);
 	} else {
